    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0697" n="683" xml:id="pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/7–2044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-07-20">July 20, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <table>
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell rendition="#top #nowrap">Participants:</cell>
                        <cell>Sr. Enrique Gajardo, Chilean Chargé d’Affaires</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Sr. Mario Rodriguez, Counselor of Chilean Embassy</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Secretary of State Hull</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>(Mr. Lyon, Acting Chief of WCA, present)</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(4)</label>
                    <item>Sr. Gajardo expressed on behalf of his Government appreciation for the
                        Lend-Lease equipment which we had in the past supplied to Chile and left
                        with me the attached memorandum,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d650-f1"/> indicating
                        that the Chilean Government wishes to build a network of airfields from the
                        extreme north to the extreme south of Chile. He explained that Chile’s
                        present airfields are totally inadequate for large modern aircraft and that
                        the Chilean Government feels that these airfields are necessary from the
                        point of view of hemispheric defense and might one day be used by the
                        airplanes of the United States. I told Sr. Gajardo that I would be glad to
                        have the appropriate officials of this Government study the question. He
                        said that if these officials were favorably impressed, he would be glad to
                        bring his experts to talk the matter over with them.</item>
                    <label>(5)</label>
                    <item>Sr. Gajardo also left with me the attached memorandum<anchor n="33"
                            xml:id="d650-f2"/> concerning the desire of the Chilean Government to
                        obtain 15 Douglas airplanes for the Chilean National Air Line. I explained
                        to Sr. Gajardo that I did not know whether these planes were available at
                        the present time but if they were not, I would have the appropriate
                        officials follow the question with a view to giving it all consideration
                        when the planes became available.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
